Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:32:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D112 model requests: one-shot calls retry a connection Bun
 reports as refused

Upstream: one-shot generations (stateless text, images, decisions) retry only failures the provider never received, recognized by the transport codes ECONNREFUSED, ENOTFOUND and EAI_AGAIN. Bun's fetch reports a refused connection as ConnectionRefused ("Unable to connect. Is the computer able to access the url?"), so under Bun a refused connection failed the call at once with a 502 ProviderRequestError instead of retrying. The same file's network-error list already names ConnectionRefused as Bun's code.
Fixed: ConnectionRefused counts as not sent, like ECONNREFUSED.
Scenarios: agent-loop-transport.test.ts "one-shot generation retries a refused connection" (now throws the error Bun's fetch throws; it ran with Node's error shape before)
Upstream tests: test/generate.test.ts ("retries a stateless call the provider never received" runs for both error shapes)

